WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:29.458 --> 00:00:31.000
But it's terrible here.

2
00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:37.833
PLANNED POWER SHUTDOWN

3
00:00:38.708 --> 00:00:40.083
I'm done.

4
00:00:46.708 --> 00:00:48.000
Not good.

5
00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:42.458
All right!

6
00:02:03.416 --> 00:02:04.416
Oh no.

7
00:02:42.041 --> 00:02:43.458
Mrs. Hana?

8
00:02:45.375 --> 00:02:47.333
What are you doing here so early?

9
00:02:51.166 --> 00:02:54.083
Well… I…

10
00:02:54.166 --> 00:02:57.000
- I think I dropped something.
- What?

11
00:02:57.583 --> 00:02:58.958
Good morning.

12
00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:01.000
- Good morning.
- Weird.

13
00:03:07.708 --> 00:03:08.708
Oh!

14
00:03:17.958 --> 00:03:21.041
Our training was about to end.

15
00:03:21.541 --> 00:03:24.458
We'd better stop practicing

16
00:03:24.958 --> 00:03:26.416
for everyone's sake.

17
00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.291
ROMANTICS ANONYMOUS

18
00:03:58.375 --> 00:04:01.583
EPISODE 7
KENJI'S ESSENCE

19
00:04:02.125 --> 00:04:03.000
Could you…

20
00:04:03.083 --> 00:04:04.250
SAVIOR SHUTDOWN PLAN

21
00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:06.458
...give the Savior another chance?

22
00:04:06.541 --> 00:04:07.500
Please.

23
00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:13.375
I've been worried about moves lately
our main shareholders.

24
00:04:15.583 --> 00:04:17.875
Even the smallest management error

25
00:04:18.375 --> 00:04:21.166
can be used against us.

26
00:04:21.666 --> 00:04:27.125
Therefore, the Savior must win
Chocolate making championship.

27
00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:30.916
We will prove that we are
the best in the world

28
00:04:31.458 --> 00:04:34.041
and we will bring profits to Futago Sweets.

29
00:04:37.416 --> 00:04:40.291
Winning the chocolatier championship?

30
00:04:41.583 --> 00:04:44.625
If you prove
that your dream is right,

31
00:04:45.875 --> 00:04:46.875
I'll think about it.

32
00:04:49.083 --> 00:04:50.291
Thank you.

33
00:05:02.416 --> 00:05:05.208
KENJI'S ESSENCE

34
00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:09.500
Please.

35
00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:11.708
Sorry.

36
00:05:13.958 --> 00:05:16.541
I brought the entry plan to the championship,

37
00:05:16.625 --> 00:05:18.625
that you mentioned.

38
00:05:18.708 --> 00:05:21.791
I brainstormed
with other confectioners.

39
00:05:21.875 --> 00:05:25.083
We want to perform
with a slightly refined version

40
00:05:25.166 --> 00:05:27.125
Sweet cherry blossom.

41
00:05:34.875 --> 00:05:37.125
It's a difficult decision

42
00:05:37.208 --> 00:05:41.416
but let's present Kenji's Essence,
The Savior's signature product.

43
00:05:44.833 --> 00:05:48.250
Does this mean that we take away
An anonymous chocolatier?

44
00:05:48.916 --> 00:05:50.083
Correct.

45
00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:56.333
The savior must win the upcoming competition.

46
00:05:56.416 --> 00:06:02.583
For this we should choose
the best of the seven chocolates.

47
00:06:13.166 --> 00:06:17.458
The boss of every store competes,
so it should be you.

48
00:06:20.291 --> 00:06:23.166
This is the first competition
since the death of Chief Kenji.

49
00:06:24.833 --> 00:06:26.875
For the Savior to win,

50
00:06:28.125 --> 00:06:33.708
we need someone this talented
like The Anonymous Chocolatier.

51
00:06:36.208 --> 00:06:37.916
I can't accept this.

52
00:06:56.291 --> 00:06:58.666
Do we really need it

53
00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:03.833
help from Anonymous Chocolatier?

54
00:07:05.833 --> 00:07:07.875
If that's the case...

55
00:07:09.708 --> 00:07:11.250
then I am…

56
00:07:12.458 --> 00:07:13.958
Boss, I heard!

57
00:07:14.041 --> 00:07:16.750
You should be the one to enter the competition.

58
00:07:16.833 --> 00:07:20.916
He's just sneaking around
and never comes to work.

59
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.333
Boss Kenji recognized him and favored him,

60
00:07:23.416 --> 00:07:26.750
but it's you and the rest of us
she did all the work!

61
00:07:26.833 --> 00:07:28.375
Exactly.

62
00:07:28.875 --> 00:07:31.875
It doesn't matter how great he is
An anonymous chocolatier

63
00:07:32.541 --> 00:07:35.208
I won't support someone I don't know.

64
00:07:35.291 --> 00:07:37.125
Me neither!

65
00:07:37.208 --> 00:07:42.958
I can't stand the thought either
that she would compete instead of me.

66
00:07:44.375 --> 00:07:48.208
But for the sake of the Savior

67
00:07:49.708 --> 00:07:51.208
we need his help.

68
00:07:53.541 --> 00:07:56.541
God. But I'm pathetic, aren't I?

69
00:07:57.166 --> 00:07:59.541
Boss, that's not the point.

70
00:08:00.166 --> 00:08:02.166
Boss, what are you doing?

71
00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:04.333
I'll go talk to the boss.

72
00:08:16.125 --> 00:08:17.583
Excuse me, Boss?

73
00:08:19.583 --> 00:08:21.375
I have something to tell you.

74
00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:25.333
I am…

75
00:08:27.833 --> 00:08:29.583
An anonymous chocolatier…

76
00:08:31.166 --> 00:08:32.000
I mean,

77
00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.625
I can contact him.

78
00:08:36.333 --> 00:08:37.791
You can?

79
00:08:37.875 --> 00:08:39.708
How?

80
00:08:39.791 --> 00:08:41.458
The truth is

81
00:08:42.041 --> 00:08:45.375
that I contact him from time to time.

82
00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:47.750
What? Really?

83
00:08:47.833 --> 00:08:48.791
Yes.

84
00:08:49.875 --> 00:08:52.291
I'm a big fan of The Being of Kenji.

85
00:08:53.958 --> 00:09:00.583
So I'll try to convince him
to share the recipe

86
00:09:01.166 --> 00:09:04.208
with the Savior team before the competition.

87
00:09:05.291 --> 00:09:10.208
But I doubt he'll come here.

88
00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:17.083
What if he taught us remotely?

89
00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:25.541
Seriously. It's my own fault.

90
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:35.000
All right.

91
00:09:46.333 --> 00:09:48.833
Okay, we can start.

92
00:09:49.333 --> 00:09:51.541
Thank you for your cooperation.

93
00:09:53.666 --> 00:09:54.500
Yes.

94
00:09:57.083 --> 00:10:00.958
Cocoa beans
it's mainly Peruvian Criollo,

95
00:10:01.041 --> 00:10:06.625
mixed with Trinitario cocoa from Koita…

96
00:10:06.708 --> 00:10:09.541
That's what he said.

97
00:10:10.916 --> 00:10:11.916
All right.

98
00:10:14.416 --> 00:10:16.750
As you all know,

99
00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:22.250
carrying out the entire process
from smoking to mixing

100
00:10:22.333 --> 00:10:24.833
it would take us four days.

101
00:10:24.916 --> 00:10:31.166
So I got it for today
ready-made chocolate blocks.

102
00:10:31.666 --> 00:10:32.541
Is he inside?

103
00:10:34.375 --> 00:10:35.500
Yes, it's here.

104
00:10:38.125 --> 00:10:38.958
Please.

105
00:10:39.458 --> 00:10:40.750
Thank you very much.

106
00:10:41.583 --> 00:10:43.541
Careful, hot.

107
00:10:50.708 --> 00:10:53.208
Now! Please check the temperature…

108
00:10:54.541 --> 00:10:57.166
That's what he said.

109
00:11:34.833 --> 00:11:37.208
This is the same Kenji Being that we know.

110
00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:39.416
What a relief.

111
00:11:40.041 --> 00:11:41.541
Very good.

112
00:11:42.041 --> 00:11:43.791
Can I try too?

113
00:11:43.875 --> 00:11:44.708
Go ahead.

114
00:11:48.291 --> 00:11:49.333
Thanks.

115
00:11:56.916 --> 00:11:58.166
It's delicious.

116
00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:26.791
Thank you for sharing
with your precious recipe.

117
00:12:26.875 --> 00:12:28.791
Thank you!

118
00:12:28.875 --> 00:12:30.041
With pleasure.

119
00:12:30.125 --> 00:12:33.125
Try to do it
the best chocolates…

120
00:12:34.416 --> 00:12:35.916
That's what he said.

121
00:12:37.916 --> 00:12:43.250
I would like to end the remote conversation
with Anonymous chocolatier.

122
00:12:43.333 --> 00:12:44.708
Thank you for talking to us.

123
00:12:44.791 --> 00:12:46.583
Thank you for the interview!

124
00:12:48.041 --> 00:12:49.500
Great job.

125
00:12:49.583 --> 00:12:50.791
Thank you.

126
00:12:50.875 --> 00:12:52.166
- Thank you.
- Thanks!

127
00:12:55.166 --> 00:12:57.250
Boss, crush the competition.

128
00:12:57.333 --> 00:12:58.583
Don't worry.

129
00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:47.750
SAVIOR SHUTDOWN PLAN

130
00:13:49.541 --> 00:13:53.125
Mr. Fujiwara, I noticed something strange.

131
00:13:53.208 --> 00:13:54.708
Yes? What is it about?

132
00:13:54.791 --> 00:13:59.666
Hana's laptop wasn't connected today
to neither side.

133
00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:04.375
I checked the laptop's private IP address.

134
00:14:04.458 --> 00:14:06.750
Even though it is connected to our Wi-Fi,

135
00:14:06.833 --> 00:14:10.125
there is no trace
today's internet access.

136
00:14:10.208 --> 00:14:13.708
What? But she gave us instructions
in real time.

137
00:14:13.791 --> 00:14:16.291
Thanks to her, we made The Essence of Kenji.

138
00:14:16.375 --> 00:14:22.000
That means Hana can teach
making Kenji's Being without any help.

139
00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.583
In other words, it's Chocolatier Anonymous.

140
00:14:28.083 --> 00:14:29.125
- What?
- What?

141
00:14:30.541 --> 00:14:31.416
What?

142
00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:34.000
Are you serious?

143
00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:36.750
Is Nowa a brilliant confectioner?

144
00:14:37.291 --> 00:14:39.291
Wait a minute.

145
00:14:39.375 --> 00:14:41.708
Even if it's true

146
00:14:42.208 --> 00:14:44.333
why lie about it all this time?

147
00:15:08.916 --> 00:15:10.583
Mrs. Hana!

148
00:15:10.666 --> 00:15:12.333
Please wait!

149
00:15:12.833 --> 00:15:16.041
Is what Takashi said
is it true?

150
00:15:16.125 --> 00:15:21.375
I just wanted to help the Savior.

151
00:15:22.416 --> 00:15:25.625
So why did you lie?

152
00:15:27.041 --> 00:15:28.166
This…

153
00:15:29.625 --> 00:15:32.291
I've tried to tell you so many times.

154
00:15:33.625 --> 00:15:36.458
So why didn't you do it?

155
00:15:36.541 --> 00:15:39.333
I couldn't trust you then.

156
00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.333
Mrs. Hano…

157
00:15:44.916 --> 00:15:49.583
How much of you is true?

158
00:15:49.666 --> 00:15:51.208
And what about you?

159
00:15:51.833 --> 00:15:54.375
You just wanted my recipe, right?

160
00:15:54.958 --> 00:15:57.750
You came to steal
Chef Kenji's recipe.

161
00:15:57.833 --> 00:16:00.500
You're going to lock up the Savior!

162
00:16:03.166 --> 00:16:05.250
I trusted you.

163
00:16:09.041 --> 00:16:11.083
No, it's not…

164
00:16:12.083 --> 00:16:16.041
I asked everyone for help,
to prevent this from happening.

165
00:16:16.125 --> 00:16:20.125
To save the Savior,
we have to win this competition.

166
00:16:22.333 --> 00:16:23.958
- Mrs. Hano.
- What happened?

167
00:16:24.458 --> 00:16:25.583
Taxi!

168
00:16:26.083 --> 00:16:27.958
We have the recipe.

169
00:16:28.666 --> 00:16:31.125
We don't need it anymore, do we?

170
00:17:43.166 --> 00:17:47.125
To save the Savior,
we have to win this competition.

171
00:18:21.625 --> 00:18:22.833
Koita.

172
00:18:22.916 --> 00:18:24.500
BANIS FARM
KOITY REPUBLIC

173
00:18:28.416 --> 00:18:32.958
Please make sure
that you are ready for the competition.

174
00:18:33.041 --> 00:18:34.375
Mr. Fujiwara.

175
00:18:35.333 --> 00:18:36.166
Yes?

176
00:18:36.666 --> 00:18:37.958
I think

177
00:18:39.166 --> 00:18:41.291
that for the future of the Savior,

178
00:18:42.208 --> 00:18:44.500
we need an Anonymous chocolatier.

179
00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:49.833
With everyone's help

180
00:18:50.333 --> 00:18:53.166
I do what I can.

181
00:18:54.458 --> 00:18:55.291
But…

182
00:18:56.875 --> 00:18:59.000
the taste is slightly different.

183
00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:04.208
Recreating the same taste
can be difficult.

184
00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:09.750
It hurts my pride
but it doesn't matter.

185
00:19:10.416 --> 00:19:17.041
It is more important to protect our lives
in the production of chocolates.

186
00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:19.208
That's why

187
00:19:20.416 --> 00:19:26.875
please help us convince Hana
to take part in the championship

188
00:19:27.458 --> 00:19:30.291
with his Kenji Being.

189
00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:33.333
Please.

190
00:19:33.916 --> 00:19:35.333
Please.

191
00:19:36.916 --> 00:19:40.125
But Hana deceived us.

192
00:19:41.083 --> 00:19:44.083
We can't forgive her
that she betrayed our trust.

193
00:19:44.166 --> 00:19:45.000
I…

194
00:19:49.333 --> 00:19:52.041
I think Hana is a good person.

195
00:19:52.625 --> 00:19:55.041
I didn't want to cheat anyone either.

196
00:19:56.166 --> 00:19:59.666
In my last job
people were talking behind my back.

197
00:20:00.666 --> 00:20:01.625
That's why

198
00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:04.875
I decided to remain silent.

199
00:20:04.958 --> 00:20:06.291
Sorry.

200
00:20:06.833 --> 00:20:08.083
You're welcome.

201
00:20:09.916 --> 00:20:11.833
But don't you think

202
00:20:12.791 --> 00:20:16.125
that we all wear masks in some way?

203
00:20:16.625 --> 00:20:17.458
Takuya…

204
00:20:18.083 --> 00:20:21.375
You really talk a lot and it's good stuff.

205
00:20:22.083 --> 00:20:24.416
Plus you have a great voice.

206
00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:26.333
He surprised me.

207
00:20:26.416 --> 00:20:27.958
Me too.

208
00:20:28.958 --> 00:20:34.000
Boss Kenji accepted me as
what I am like.

209
00:20:36.208 --> 00:20:40.666
He said, "Here in the Savior,
you can be whoever you want.

210
00:20:41.833 --> 00:20:44.625
You don't need words
to make chocolates.

211
00:20:45.208 --> 00:20:47.458
Your heart is enough.”

212
00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:50.666
That's why I feel

213
00:20:52.291 --> 00:20:55.375
in the Savior happy.

214
00:20:56.375 --> 00:20:59.708
Because everyone
you accepted me as I am...

215
00:21:01.791 --> 00:21:05.375
I'm slowly recovering
after my emotional problems.

216
00:21:10.333 --> 00:21:11.791
I think it's for Hana

217
00:21:13.666 --> 00:21:17.291
The Savior was such a place too.

218
00:21:19.666 --> 00:21:24.583
Hana apologized to us sincerely.

219
00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:35.958
To my family in the Savior.

220
00:21:37.666 --> 00:21:39.208
Good morning.

221
00:21:39.291 --> 00:21:44.583
I have suffered from scopophobia since I was a child

222
00:21:44.666 --> 00:21:47.750
and I can't stand in front of you all.

223
00:21:49.041 --> 00:21:53.958
That's why I hope I can make it
convey my feelings through this letter.

224
00:21:55.875 --> 00:21:59.791
For a long time
I was boss Kenji's apprentice.

225
00:22:00.291 --> 00:22:03.916
I am anonymous
chocolatier, Lee Han.

226
00:22:05.916 --> 00:22:09.666
Working with everyone at Savior

227
00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:11.750
it's real joy.

228
00:22:13.333 --> 00:22:15.541
I never wanted to cheat you.

229
00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:19.333
Because of my illness

230
00:22:19.416 --> 00:22:23.166
I've always lived my life
looking away from the world.

231
00:22:23.666 --> 00:22:26.875
I lacked self-confidence

232
00:22:27.375 --> 00:22:31.500
and I thought no one would love me.

233
00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:36.708
But when I met you

234
00:22:37.333 --> 00:22:39.583
and I worked with you every day,

235
00:22:40.083 --> 00:22:46.416
for the first time in my life I felt
as if I had another family.

236
00:22:47.583 --> 00:22:53.416
That's why I wanted to stay
in this family circle.

237
00:22:55.125 --> 00:22:58.250
This feeling wasn't a lie.

238
00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:01.500
Thank you very much.

239
00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:03.791
I am truly grateful to you.

240
00:23:04.375 --> 00:23:07.166
We may never meet again

241
00:23:07.666 --> 00:23:09.583
but I will never forget you.

242
00:23:18.125 --> 00:23:21.458
She's my employee with no family.
I'll check if she's okay.

243
00:23:21.541 --> 00:23:22.708
I see.

244
00:23:24.541 --> 00:23:25.916
Thank you.

245
00:23:57.333 --> 00:23:58.583
She was here…

246
00:24:01.708 --> 00:24:03.583
alone all this time.

247
00:24:37.333 --> 00:24:40.291
When I was in the Koita Republic,

248
00:24:40.875 --> 00:24:44.375
I heard about rare cocoa,
from which the best chocolate is made.

249
00:24:44.458 --> 00:24:47.916
It was called "a gift from heaven."

250
00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:53.041
I thought maybe cocoa,
that Boss Kenji keeps here,

251
00:24:53.125 --> 00:24:55.458
that's it.

252
00:24:55.958 --> 00:24:58.333
They also call it "purple cocoa".

253
00:24:58.833 --> 00:24:59.666
Well,

254
00:25:00.791 --> 00:25:02.916
we won't see it in this photo.

255
00:25:19.875 --> 00:25:20.875
I feed…

256
00:25:22.083 --> 00:25:23.875
feelings for someone.

257
00:25:26.041 --> 00:25:28.791
But she always runs away from me.

258
00:25:33.958 --> 00:25:35.333
My mother…

259
00:25:38.541 --> 00:25:39.791
she was an alcoholic.

260
00:25:41.625 --> 00:25:44.041
Because my father beat her every day

261
00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:48.375
she became addicted,
although she couldn't tolerate alcohol.

262
00:25:51.583 --> 00:25:55.541
When I was little, she left me and disappeared.

263
00:25:56.791 --> 00:25:59.625
I hated myself for it
that I couldn't do anything.

264
00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:02.500
When I see this person...

265
00:26:04.625 --> 00:26:06.291
reminds me of my mother.

266
00:26:07.750 --> 00:26:09.833
She's a different person when she's drunk

267
00:26:10.333 --> 00:26:11.708
but she is beautiful...

268
00:26:13.916 --> 00:26:16.166
And he has a heart of gold.

269
00:26:19.125 --> 00:26:20.291
Recently…

270
00:26:23.208 --> 00:26:24.416
I was wondering

271
00:26:26.166 --> 00:26:29.000
Or am I broken inside?

272
00:26:31.583 --> 00:26:32.875
Just like her.

273
00:26:34.750 --> 00:26:37.125
But I decided to forget about the past

274
00:26:37.750 --> 00:26:42.750
and choose your own future.

275
00:26:55.125 --> 00:26:58.125
Let's end this.

276
00:27:00.166 --> 00:27:03.708
This will be best.

277
00:27:09.458 --> 00:27:13.625
I'm sorry for everything so far.

278
00:27:28.833 --> 00:27:29.666
What is this?

279
00:27:30.708 --> 00:27:37.708
Hana probably succeeded
to the Koita Republic for cocoa.

280
00:27:38.708 --> 00:27:40.458
Bring her here.

281
00:27:42.416 --> 00:27:43.250
Wait…

282
00:27:44.416 --> 00:27:48.125
Why… me?

283
00:27:52.916 --> 00:27:54.125
One day…

284
00:27:56.916 --> 00:28:01.041
I saw you kissing.

285
00:28:04.125 --> 00:28:05.833
What? When?

286
00:28:05.916 --> 00:28:08.000
A few days ago. Here.

287
00:28:15.291 --> 00:28:16.250
Seriously?

288
00:28:30.666 --> 00:28:31.916
Irene…

289
00:28:36.625 --> 00:28:38.666
Are you okay?

290
00:28:38.750 --> 00:28:40.208
Wait.

291
00:28:57.000 --> 00:29:00.500
I came to pick up my coat,

292
00:29:01.541 --> 00:29:03.875
but you were drunk and asleep.

293
00:29:06.083 --> 00:29:07.416
Sorry.

294
00:29:08.041 --> 00:29:13.125
I drank too much. I don't remember anything.

295
00:29:13.208 --> 00:29:14.250
Sorry.

296
00:29:15.333 --> 00:29:16.625
All right.

297
00:29:17.125 --> 00:29:19.083
Instead of apologizing…

298
00:29:27.041 --> 00:29:32.416
tell her how you really feel.

299
00:29:36.416 --> 00:29:39.375
You have to gather your courage

300
00:29:41.333 --> 00:29:44.500
and express your feelings to the person
which one you like.

301
00:29:48.708 --> 00:29:49.708
Me too...

302
00:29:52.125 --> 00:29:53.583
I gained courage...

303
00:29:55.583 --> 00:29:57.291
and I'll say it now.

304
00:30:00.125 --> 00:30:01.291
Always

305
00:30:03.083 --> 00:30:06.500
I was attracted to you.

306
00:30:10.208 --> 00:30:13.583
I was attracted to you?

307
00:30:14.166 --> 00:30:17.458
You probably don't remember this.

308
00:30:18.500 --> 00:30:23.250
When I almost had an accident outside,

309
00:30:24.250 --> 00:30:26.333
you saved me.

310
00:30:27.375 --> 00:30:31.500
It's embarrassing, but since then

311
00:30:32.791 --> 00:30:34.916
I wanted to see you.

312
00:30:37.291 --> 00:30:39.166
I even started learning kendo.

313
00:30:40.083 --> 00:30:40.916
alone,

314
00:30:42.833 --> 00:30:44.958
in my own world…

315
00:30:47.041 --> 00:30:51.875
I fell in love with you.

316
00:30:53.625 --> 00:30:55.333
I liked you.

317
00:30:57.625 --> 00:30:59.791
Did you like me?

318
00:31:00.708 --> 00:31:03.500
Thanks to you, I understood something.

319
00:31:05.500 --> 00:31:09.333
Now I feel grateful.

320
00:31:10.375 --> 00:31:11.250
Yes.

321
00:31:15.083 --> 00:31:20.416
Thank you for everything so far.

322
00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:32.166
Your eyes

323
00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:37.291
they're always looking for Sosuke, right?

324
00:31:38.500 --> 00:31:41.708
Feelings that get so strong
that you can't hide them

325
00:31:42.458 --> 00:31:46.666
sometimes they are more visible
for the people around you.

326
00:31:48.458 --> 00:31:49.708
And…

327
00:31:52.083 --> 00:31:55.125
I guess it wasn't me

328
00:31:55.958 --> 00:31:57.958
who saved you.

329
00:31:59.916 --> 00:32:00.833
What?

330
00:32:06.375 --> 00:32:07.708
It's dangerous.

331
00:32:07.791 --> 00:32:09.541
TAKADA

332
00:32:09.625 --> 00:32:10.875
Hello?

333
00:32:10.958 --> 00:32:12.250
I'm fine.

334
00:32:13.083 --> 00:32:14.875
I'm almost there.

335
00:32:19.750 --> 00:32:24.708
Do you remember when you brought it to me?
new kendo equipment for your birthday?

336
00:32:25.708 --> 00:32:28.000
You said you saved someone that time.

337
00:32:29.125 --> 00:32:31.291
It turns out it was Hana.

338
00:32:32.166 --> 00:32:34.916
Are you idiots or what?

339
00:32:35.791 --> 00:32:36.625
What?

340
00:32:37.750 --> 00:32:39.916
It's you that Hana likes.

341
00:32:41.208 --> 00:32:42.333
Me?

342
00:32:43.083 --> 00:32:44.000
Yes.

343
00:32:44.083 --> 00:32:47.166
For some time now.

344
00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:08.083
Always keep your bag closed.

345
00:33:09.833 --> 00:33:10.833
Thank you.

346
00:33:37.708 --> 00:33:39.375
Thief!

347
00:33:39.458 --> 00:33:40.916
Oh no!

348
00:33:48.125 --> 00:33:51.000
Sorry, that bastard was fast.

349
00:33:51.500 --> 00:33:53.791
- Thank you.
- Was there anything important there?

350
00:33:57.583 --> 00:33:59.708
I still have my wallet and phone.

351
00:33:59.791 --> 00:34:02.125
Good to know.

352
00:34:03.958 --> 00:34:08.541
I'm actually looking for something.

353
00:34:09.708 --> 00:34:11.458
Have you seen this place?

354
00:34:14.625 --> 00:34:16.791
Yes. Follow me.

355
00:34:16.875 --> 00:34:18.166
Wait.

356
00:34:19.125 --> 00:34:20.875
- Really?
- Come.

357
00:34:22.041 --> 00:34:23.041
Do you really know?

358
00:34:23.125 --> 00:34:24.375
Really.

359
00:34:37.500 --> 00:34:38.875
I found it!

360
00:34:40.000 --> 00:34:41.458
Come this way.

361
00:34:41.541 --> 00:34:43.208
Yes! All right!

362
00:34:45.000 --> 00:34:47.875
Banis Farm? I grew up there.

363
00:34:49.541 --> 00:34:52.333
But are you sure you want to go there?

364
00:34:52.875 --> 00:34:54.583
Is this a problem?

365
00:34:56.375 --> 00:34:58.833
Unfortunately, it's a dangerous place now.

366
00:34:58.916 --> 00:35:01.083
Strangers are not welcome there.

367
00:35:04.958 --> 00:35:05.958
I see.

368
00:35:06.916 --> 00:35:07.916
Come.

369
00:35:15.291 --> 00:35:17.458
All right. Come.

370
00:35:36.166 --> 00:35:38.375
Okay, give me everything you have.

371
00:35:38.958 --> 00:35:41.166
Wallet, passport, everything.

372
00:35:41.250 --> 00:35:42.458
- NO!
- Faster!

373
00:35:42.541 --> 00:35:44.041
Before the police arrive.

374
00:35:44.541 --> 00:35:46.416
Give us everything and get out.

375
00:35:46.500 --> 00:35:49.416
Miss. You understand?

376
00:35:49.500 --> 00:35:51.708
I have no money!

377
00:35:51.791 --> 00:35:53.458
Leave everything you have!

378
00:35:53.541 --> 00:35:55.416
Let me go please!

379
00:35:55.500 --> 00:35:56.958
NO!

380
00:35:57.041 --> 00:35:59.291
Next. Hurry up.

381
00:35:59.375 --> 00:36:00.958
Give us everything. Already!

382
00:36:04.708 --> 00:36:05.833
Hana!

383
00:36:58.541 --> 00:36:59.708
Why?

384
00:37:00.208 --> 00:37:03.375
Quiet. You are safe now.

385
00:37:09.916 --> 00:37:11.083
Are you injured?

386
00:37:11.916 --> 00:37:14.041
Why did you come here alone?

387
00:37:16.083 --> 00:37:21.250
I just wanted to help everyone.

388
00:37:23.833 --> 00:37:24.916
It's okay.

389
00:37:37.083 --> 00:37:38.291
- Mr. Fujiwara!
- What?

390
00:37:38.375 --> 00:37:39.875
Are you okay?

391
00:37:40.375 --> 00:37:42.083
Everything's all right?

392
00:37:42.166 --> 00:37:43.166
What?

393
00:37:48.958 --> 00:37:49.958
Thank you.

394
00:37:50.041 --> 00:37:50.916
Be careful.

395
00:37:56.083 --> 00:37:57.333
Everything's all right?

396
00:37:57.416 --> 00:37:59.500
Why did you get hurt?

397
00:37:59.583 --> 00:38:01.458
I was really worried!

398
00:38:01.541 --> 00:38:04.208
I'm fine. It's just a scratch.

399
00:38:04.708 --> 00:38:07.166
More importantly,

400
00:38:07.916 --> 00:38:09.708
what did you just say?

401
00:38:10.791 --> 00:38:11.750
What?

402
00:38:11.833 --> 00:38:16.625
You said you really did
worried about me?

403
00:38:17.708 --> 00:38:18.791
Well…

404
00:38:21.458 --> 00:38:23.041
It's natural!

405
00:38:23.125 --> 00:38:25.666
You suffered because of me.

406
00:38:27.750 --> 00:38:28.833
Anyway,

407
00:38:29.583 --> 00:38:31.750
why did you leave without saying a word?

408
00:38:33.125 --> 00:38:35.458
Don't disappear from my sight ever again.

409
00:38:42.166 --> 00:38:43.000
I mean…

410
00:38:46.333 --> 00:38:52.333
As your boss, I'm in trouble
when my employee suddenly disappears.

411
00:38:53.541 --> 00:38:56.708
But I'm no longer your employee.

412
00:38:58.416 --> 00:39:00.500
I see.

413
00:39:01.541 --> 00:39:04.166
You are no longer my employee.

414
00:39:05.500 --> 00:39:10.833
But that's different
if you are an Anonymous chocolatier.

415
00:39:11.416 --> 00:39:15.041
I'm also here on business.

416
00:39:15.875 --> 00:39:20.333
To ask the best chocolatier
in Japan with brilliant skills,

417
00:39:21.791 --> 00:39:26.166
to make the best chocolate
for the upcoming competition.

418
00:39:31.333 --> 00:39:35.875
I'm Sosuke Fujiwara, president of the Savior.

419
00:39:37.208 --> 00:39:39.958
Will you represent the Savior?

420
00:39:40.875 --> 00:39:43.708
and compete
in the Chocolatier Championship?

421
00:39:48.208 --> 00:39:49.333
Please.

422
00:40:07.708 --> 00:40:08.583
It hurts.

423
00:40:10.416 --> 00:40:13.625
- Are you okay?
- NO.

424
00:40:16.500 --> 00:40:20.750
You seem hungry,
so let's go eat something.

425
00:40:22.083 --> 00:40:23.000
All right.

426
00:40:23.666 --> 00:40:25.083
I'm hungry.

427
00:40:30.916 --> 00:40:32.291
This is delicious too.

428
00:40:32.875 --> 00:40:33.875
What is this?

429
00:40:33.958 --> 00:40:36.416
You seem to like it.

430
00:40:36.916 --> 00:40:38.125
Very good.

431
00:40:39.375 --> 00:40:40.416
Enjoy your meal.

432
00:40:40.500 --> 00:40:42.000
Thank you very much.

433
00:40:43.500 --> 00:40:45.333
There's still a lot left.

434
00:40:46.041 --> 00:40:48.791
Sorry about earlier.

435
00:40:49.500 --> 00:40:52.250
I was only thinking about myself again.

436
00:40:53.791 --> 00:40:58.833
I thought winning and proving it
our skills will save the Savior.

437
00:40:59.500 --> 00:41:00.458
NO.

438
00:41:02.666 --> 00:41:03.958
If I run,

439
00:41:04.916 --> 00:41:09.375
instead I can ruin everything.

440
00:41:10.333 --> 00:41:12.083
I can escape from there...

441
00:41:15.708 --> 00:41:18.333
and not think about winning.

442
00:41:20.375 --> 00:41:23.083
Therefore, for the sake of the Savior

443
00:41:24.250 --> 00:41:27.666
at all costs
I had to find a godsend.

444
00:41:29.125 --> 00:41:30.708
Still

445
00:41:32.333 --> 00:41:35.375
who comes to such a place alone?

446
00:41:35.458 --> 00:41:38.291
No feeling of fear
and only with one photo.

447
00:41:39.833 --> 00:41:42.166
As if you came looking for a miracle.

448
00:41:45.041 --> 00:41:46.916
Miracle

449
00:41:47.916 --> 00:41:50.666
it's something that happens at the end.

450
00:41:51.916 --> 00:41:55.208
I think that's why the word "miracle" exists.

451
00:42:00.708 --> 00:42:02.458
You were serious, right?

452
00:42:04.791 --> 00:42:08.208
That you want to save the Savior?

453
00:42:12.333 --> 00:42:13.166
Yes.

454
00:42:14.625 --> 00:42:20.833
So no matter what
let's find this miracle together.

455
00:42:23.708 --> 00:42:24.541
Yes.

456
00:42:29.875 --> 00:42:31.416
You're lucky!

457
00:42:32.250 --> 00:42:35.041
If Mrs. Hana hadn't been hungry,
we might not come here.

458
00:42:35.125 --> 00:42:37.375
I talked to the owner. You know what?

459
00:42:37.875 --> 00:42:41.541
He said it was his relative
she was the owner of Banis Farm!

460
00:42:52.375 --> 00:42:53.833
I remember him.

461
00:42:56.000 --> 00:43:00.000
His chocolate was so good.

462
00:43:00.583 --> 00:43:03.666
His name was Kenji, right?

463
00:43:03.750 --> 00:43:05.916
Yes! Kenji!

464
00:43:06.500 --> 00:43:09.458
Do you know anything about that cocoa she's holding?

465
00:43:09.541 --> 00:43:10.583
A godsend?

466
00:43:11.458 --> 00:43:12.541
This fruit?

467
00:43:14.333 --> 00:43:16.666
He holds a rotten fruit.

468
00:43:16.750 --> 00:43:17.958
I'm listening?

469
00:43:18.750 --> 00:43:21.583
In the first year of the farm's operation

470
00:43:22.083 --> 00:43:24.458
a cocoa disease appeared.

471
00:43:25.666 --> 00:43:28.875
Everything rotted.

472
00:43:29.500 --> 00:43:31.875
Those fruits were for testing purposes.

473
00:43:32.625 --> 00:43:36.958
Defective creations sent by God.

474
00:43:37.458 --> 00:43:42.250
But Kenji suggested
that he will buy our cocoa,

475
00:43:42.333 --> 00:43:45.291
if we can save the good parts.

476
00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:48.125
It was a real miracle.

477
00:43:49.375 --> 00:43:51.416
Come here!

478
00:43:56.791 --> 00:44:00.416
We worked for many years
on cocoa plantations,

479
00:44:00.500 --> 00:44:05.166
but we have never tried chocolates
from our cocoa.

480
00:44:07.583 --> 00:44:09.916
Everyone cried.

481
00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:13.875
It was the best chocolate
what we ate.

482
00:44:13.958 --> 00:44:15.000
Enjoy your meal!

483
00:44:15.083 --> 00:44:16.083
She's so good.

484
00:44:16.166 --> 00:44:17.250
Yes.

485
00:44:21.958 --> 00:44:23.875
Kenji made us proud

486
00:44:25.416 --> 00:44:29.416
from our own work.

487
00:44:44.833 --> 00:44:46.291
Here she is.

488
00:44:46.958 --> 00:44:49.250
Kenji's chocolate.

489
00:44:56.166 --> 00:44:58.833
"Le chocolat du Bonheur."

490
00:45:03.083 --> 00:45:05.458
Chocolate of happiness.

491
00:45:07.291 --> 00:45:10.500
Chocolate of happiness.

492
00:45:18.375 --> 00:45:23.416
This old lady looked happy,
when she was talking about Chef Kenji's chocolate.

493
00:45:24.041 --> 00:45:24.875
Yes.

494
00:45:26.166 --> 00:45:29.000
Slightly spoiled and damaged fruit

495
00:45:29.083 --> 00:45:31.916
they were actually a gift from God.

496
00:45:32.791 --> 00:45:34.875
It was a real miracle.

497
00:45:40.625 --> 00:45:43.291
Even though I'm a bit spoiled

498
00:45:45.208 --> 00:45:47.708
if you accept
someone like me...

499
00:45:51.791 --> 00:45:54.750
I will take part in the competition.

500
00:45:59.000 --> 00:46:01.666
If in order to save the store,
please don't force yourself.

501
00:46:01.750 --> 00:46:02.583
NO.

502
00:46:03.583 --> 00:46:07.333
I'm not doing this for anyone
only for yourself.

503
00:46:08.416 --> 00:46:11.875
I don't want to hide anymore.

504
00:46:12.375 --> 00:46:14.000
I'm tired of running away.

505
00:46:18.166 --> 00:46:20.791
Are you sure you can handle it?

506
00:46:21.375 --> 00:46:22.208
Of course

507
00:46:23.041 --> 00:46:25.291
I won't feel well.

508
00:46:28.958 --> 00:46:31.083
I want it to be good

509
00:46:31.708 --> 00:46:35.875
but that itself seems like a miracle.

510
00:46:38.750 --> 00:46:42.208
“A miracle is something that happens at the end.

511
00:46:43.041 --> 00:46:46.833
That's why the word "miracle" exists.

512
00:46:46.916 --> 00:46:49.000
Has anyone said anything like that?

513
00:46:51.541 --> 00:46:55.875
Even if a miracle doesn't happen...

514
00:46:57.916 --> 00:46:59.708
I'll be there for you.

515
00:47:00.583 --> 00:47:02.916
Wherever you look, I will be there.

516
00:47:08.250 --> 00:47:09.208
So…

517
00:47:14.416 --> 00:47:16.166
I rely on you.

518
00:48:00.166 --> 00:48:04.458
You said we didn't have to practice anymore.

519
00:48:05.291 --> 00:48:06.166
Yes.

520
00:48:07.291 --> 00:48:09.208
We don't have to practice anymore.

521
00:48:10.583 --> 00:48:11.625
So…

522
00:48:13.166 --> 00:48:15.666
I'll be the first to pluck up the courage.

523
00:48:18.791 --> 00:48:20.625
These are not exercises.

524
00:48:22.625 --> 00:48:23.500
Sarang.

525
00:48:33.583 --> 00:48:34.500
Sarang.

526
00:48:40.583 --> 00:48:41.416
What?

527
00:49:08.416 --> 00:49:12.708
Thank you all for your hard work.

528
00:49:13.708 --> 00:49:15.666
The day has finally come.

529
00:49:16.416 --> 00:49:19.208
Our fund will buy the company's shares,

530
00:49:19.708 --> 00:49:22.166
and you will take over.

531
00:49:22.250 --> 00:49:24.791
I will return the favor with a large profit.

532
00:49:24.875 --> 00:49:27.000
Please focus on redemption.

533
00:49:27.833 --> 00:49:32.333
Let's make sure everything runs smoothly,
until trading starts.

534
00:49:32.416 --> 00:49:33.625
Yes Sir.

535
00:49:38.750 --> 00:49:40.666
Yes. I see.

536
00:49:41.541 --> 00:49:43.708
This shouldn't be a problem.

537
00:49:44.583 --> 00:49:45.416
Yes.

538
00:49:45.916 --> 00:49:47.041
See you tomorrow.

539
00:54:11.250 --> 00:54:14.083
Subtitles: Grzegorz Marczyk

